CHAPTER.VERS:
If there should be famine upon the land, if there should be death, a pestilent wind an blight; if there should be locust and 

          Gr. blight, or itch
         caterpiller, and if the enemy should harass them before their cities: in whatever plague and whatever distress they may be;

and if they shall 

          Gr. turn their heart
         repent in their land whither they were carried captive, and shall also turn and make supplication to thee in their captivity, saying, We have sinned, we have transgressed, we have wrought unrighteously;
